        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 78-year-old male patient, admitted on 29/07/2018 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing a mild inflammatory response. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout his stay. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 30/07/2018 with oral prednisolone, inhaled bronchodilators, and instructions for follow-up spirometry. Please arrange early outpatient review and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral.</div>"
            },
